Looking at the demos, the rule is: each grid has two bands, each with an edge "line" of one color, and scatter cells of another color in one band. In rows with scatter, cells between the line and the scatter become the scatter color and the scatter cell becomes 4. In the other band, the corresponding rows (same offset from band start as scatter rows) are filled entirely with the scatter color.

Applying this: scatter color 7, lines of 3 at col5 (rows 0–3) and col0 (rows 19–23), scatters at rows 20–23 mapping to top rows 0–3.

